--  Read by a conformance case that runs this shell from this shell.
--
--  A script that a user runs may well run another, and until something asserts
--  it nobody knows whether it works on every host: a shell started by a shell
--  is a child like any other, but it is the only child that reads a script,
--  writes to a captured pipe, and exits with a status of its own.
put_line ("from the child");
put_line ("and again");
quit (0);
